(kicad_sch
	(version 20260306)
	(generator "aed_schgen")
	(generator_version "1.0")
	(uuid "6770f478-041d-58cc-9194-17614ebcfd25")
	(paper "A0")
	(title_block
		(title "HIGH VOLTAGE: storage terminals, bleeder, sense strings, discharge stacks A/B, hold pumps, held sense, OVP force")
		(date "2026-11-27")
		(rev "A-draft")
		(company "Open AED project — CERN-OHL-S-2.0 — NOT FOR CONSTRUCTION")
		(comment 1 "NOT FOR CONSTRUCTION — unreviewed design")
		(comment 2 "Source: docs/HARDWARE_DESIGN.md v0.3 §B5, §B9.1; contract.md issue 3 §5.4-5.6, §8 sheet 11; capture-notes/rev3-changes.md WP-F; capture notes WP-F.md")
		(comment 3 "HIGH VOLTAGE up to 2,200 V on HV_CAP_P and every HV_* net. A charged capacitor must always have a way to empty: two independent depletion stacks (A held off only by the main, B only by the supervisor) plus a permanent bleeder.")
		(comment 4 "Held = an optocoupler LED lit by the negative gate bias (R-6); TWO independent sensors per stack, each on its own line (rev 0.3, I-4). Open, unpowered or missing = not held. Over-voltage force = a further opto per stack shorting the bias (R-10).")
		(comment 5 "Rev 0.3: 1,700 V IXTT2N170D2 devices, steered upper gates (GP02-40 || 22 M, 100 M gate-source), 4 x (2 x 10 M) string (WP-F W-1), 10 M + 3.3 nF across every device, 470 ohm pump output, MMBFJ270 pilots, 4.3 V zeners. Capture WP-F 2026-11-27; departures and simulations in hardware/aed-main/capture-notes/WP-F.md.")
		(comment 6 "Generated by tools/schgen from the sheet spec — edit the spec, not this file (until schematic freeze)")
	)
