	(text_box "Capacitor terminals J1101, case-NTC connector J1102, HV_RTN-GND star ties NT1101 || NT1102"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 25.4 0)
		(size 156.2 5.35)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "863ff4b3-2a8f-5e03-88d4-286959f3e2b1")
	)
	(text_box "C1101 (the made-to-order 100 uF / >= 2,200 V film capacitor, PARTS_STUDY Appendix A) is OFF-BOARD on J1101 and is not drawn as a part.\nHV_RTN is the capacitor negative and the source of both stacks; it meets GND only at the two net ties, built as two separate wide bonds\nso one open bond does not separate them (R-9, fault 11). Every circuit on this sheet that must keep working if they did separate (hold\npumps, held sensing, OVP force) is coupled to the GND side by capacitors or light only. J1102 carries the two independent case NTCs (one\nper controller, D-56); each NTC has its own GND return pin."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 31.75 0)
		(size 156.2 12.795)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "c5483089-152c-5cc5-9090-9c6886a50128")
	)
	(text_box "Permanent bleeder: 8 x 2.49 Mohm (19.9 Mohm), always connected, its own string"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 201.92 25.4 0)
		(size 255.15 5.35)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "299347b9-83c8-5a13-bdf6-3228240282b7")
	)
	(text_box "Last-resort discharge (§B5.6). 273 V and 30 mW per element at 2,182 V. With everything always connected (bleeder, both sense strings, both sharing strings) the capacitor falls from 2,008 V to 50 V in about 41 min; bleeder\nalone about 2.0 h (arithmetic in WP-F.md)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 201.92 31.75 0)
		(size 255.15 6.318)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "ea80c9d6-cfbf-5de0-ac48-5be82dab7026")
	)
	(text_box "Main capacitor-voltage string -> VCAP_M_TAP (1:998, Stackpole HVCR, to 07)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 477.39 25.4 0)
		(size 256.06 5.35)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "349163a0-538c-551e-97c0-25e40c061d18")
	)
	(text_box "10 x 4.02 Mohm HVCR2512 + bottom leg 2 x 80.6 kohm in parallel (40.3 kohm) to HV_RTN: ratio (40.2 M + 40.3 k)/40.3 k = 998.5. Tap clamp per R-21: 10 kohm series + TPD1E01B04 (3.6 V stand-off, <= 10 nA at 2.5 V) to GND, not to\na reader's rail. One bottom-leg resistor open doubles the reading (R-27). 4.02 Mohm is NOT in the HVCR standard value list (10 M-100 M, rev 9/22/2025): availability to confirm with Stackpole (WP-F.md, contract issue C-2)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 477.39 31.75 0)
		(size 256.06 6.318)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "5b2338ee-eedb-5136-81bd-d041e96bbaa3")
	)
	(text_box "Supervisor capacitor-voltage string -> VCAP_S_TAP (1:1,001, Vishay TNPV thin film, to 08)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 753.77 25.4 0)
		(size 267.56 5.35)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "6e8d2632-d3d5-5ad0-bdb8-e6d91d19b489")
	)
	(text_box "20 x 1.99 Mohm TNPV1206 (0.1 %, 25 ppm/K, < 1 ppm/V) + bottom leg 2 x 79.6 kohm TNPW1206 in parallel: ratio (39.8 M + 39.8 k)/39.8 k = 1,001. DEPARTURE: the contract names 12 x 3.32 Mohm TNPV1206, but TNPV1206 stops at 2.0 Mohm\n(datasheet 28881, 29-Apr-2026); same total resistance, 109 V per element. Shares no part, maker or footprint row with the main string or the bleeder (D-28). Tap clamp as the main string."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 753.77 31.75 0)
		(size 267.56 6.318)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "ca8a0885-404a-59b9-9b32-a31ab26191c6")
	)
	(text_box "STACK A (held off only by the MAIN): dump resistors R1101-R1103 + Q1101 (bottom) ... Q1104 (top) IXTT2N170D2, steered gate feeds, sharing string, per-device RC, gate clamps"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 90.265 0)
		(size 293.96 5.35)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "2fe4fa37-9805-54a6-be43-509350203ffc")
	)
	(text_box "Normally ON: with no gate bias every IXTT2N170D2 (1,700 V) conducts (VGS = 0, RDS(on) <= 6.5 ohm) and the capacitor empties through 3 x 1.5 kohm. Rev 0.3 (cfg 5 of sim/charger-storage, I-3): sharing string of 4 elements, each 2 x 10 Mohm in parallel (5.0 Mohm;\nWP-F change W-1 replaces the change order's single 4.7 Mohm so that one open resistor cannot remove a tap reference), + 3.3 nF per element; each upper gate fed tap -> 100 k -> GP02-40 steering diode (anode at the tap side) bypassed by 22 Mohm -> gate, 100 Mohm\ngate-source, 15 V TVS gate-source; and 10 Mohm + 3.3 nF directly across EVERY device (essential: with a steered gate a leaky device's source can float). The diode stops a shorted device's clamp current from dragging the tap below, so one shorted device puts\nabout V/2 on a neighbour instead of nearly all of it [SIM]. The v0.2 figure of 727 V with one device shorted was wrong (I-3). Results and margins: WP-F.md, Revision 0.3."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 96.615 0)
		(size 293.96 10.636)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "90a177db-f112-524a-a96b-52b1e4d3657d")
	)
	(text_box "Stack A hold: HOLD_A_DRV (1.5 kHz) -> 4-stage pump -> 470 ohm -> bottom gate STKA_G; release Q1109 with MMBFJ270 pilot; two held optos U1101/U1105 -> HOLD_A_HELD_N / HOLD_A_HELD2_N"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 339.68 112.378 0)
		(size 307.4 5.35)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "6f48458d-b266-5b88-ad7a-516d2bbb352d")
	)
	(text_box "Everything here is referenced to HV_RTN at the stack and coupled to the GND side only through the pump capacitors and the optocouplers (R-9). Pump: 4-stage single-clock, BAT54S pairs, 2.2 uF; last stage PMPA_H4 -> R1194 470 ohm -> STKA_G (rev 0.3, breaks the cold power-up\nlock-out); reservoir 3.3 uF; 1.01 Mohm gate-source with 1/3 test tap. Requirement (rev 0.3): BOTH sensors held, HELD_N <= 1.0 V, at -20 C, 3.1 V clock, 1.35-1.65 kHz, aged sensors (met [SIM]); release <= 25 ms with the clock stopped LOW (firmware rule). Release: MMBFJ270\nP-JFET pilot (VGS(off) 0.5-2.0 V), normally on, pinched off only while the 3-stage BAV199 pump biases it; when the clock stops it turns on Q1109 (BSS138), which empties the gate. Held sense, two identical independent strings: HV_RTN - 3.9 k - MMSZ4687 4.3 V - TLP187 LED\n(22 k across) - STKA_G; each reads held only below about -4.95..-6.12 V [SIM]; each Darlington on its own line to 09, HOLD_OK = all four lines low. Open, unlit or unpowered = high = not held."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 339.68 118.728 0)
		(size 307.4 10.636)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -1)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "450a69e7-8c95-5f8a-aa33-4ef36c890ee8")
	)
	(text_box "STACK B (held off only by the SUPERVISOR): dump resistors R1104-R1106 + Q1105 (bottom) ... Q1108 (top) IXTT2N170D2, steered gate feeds, sharing string, per-device RC, gate clamps"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 667.4 142.858 0)
